WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.540
Inside your app, one conductor runs the work.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.570
You want a progress panel in the lobby.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.240
Tock volunteers.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.410
The quick fix copies the conductor out front.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.230
Two loops now keep time.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.020
Cancel stops only the copy.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.290
Build with Amplifier finds the right seam first, in the host you actually installed.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:30.100
The lobby owns the display and the cancel button.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:31.860
Core keeps the conductor.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.760
So you hang a hook by the podium.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.390
The lobby listens, and the work stays in the hall.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.910
Then you prove the slice: success, bad input, cancel, and cleanup.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.770
Old examples are history.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.030
You check them against what you installed.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.810
Build with Amplifier.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.170
Add the capability.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.150
Keep the architecture clear.
